<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salchak Toka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/1973">1973</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salchak Toka was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuvan-peoples-revolutionary-party">Tuvan People's Revolutionary Party</a> from 1932. He ran a Stalinist regime in the Tuvan People's Republic, collectivising herds, closing monasteries and persecuting lamas, and oversaw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuva">Tuva</a>'s annexation by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1944. He continued to lead the Tuvan communist party until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salchak-toka.jpg" alt="Salchak Toka" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salchak_toka.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
